{
  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, scvi_n200, singleprofile) achieves 0.5203 acc, and config_051 (multimodal, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, concat) improves to 0.5321 acc / 0.5172 F1, showing a modest but consistent multimodal gain. Image-only (config_010) is very weak (0.2266), confirming RNA dominates. Uncertainty: it is unclear whether the concat fusion in config_051 is optimal or whether a weighted fusion would better calibrate the contribution of the weak image signal. This experiment (config_038) changes only the fusion method (concat → weighted) while holding RNA encoder, image encoder, and profile setting identical to config_051, providing a clean single-variable A/B test. If weighted fusion outperforms concat, it indicates the image branch is noisy and should be downweighted, directly informing all future multimodal designs. If concat remains better, the image signal is additive and the fusion choice is less critical. Under a tight budget, isolating this one design decision from the already-validated baseline is the most informative next step before exploring additional axes (image encoder, multiprofile, RNA encoder)."
}

